From: paul <p4ulcristian@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8112-j413: enable SIO for DP-alt audio

The MacBook Air (M2, j413) gets DisplayPort-altmode *video* from the
ENABLE_DCPEXT_TYPEC hack in t8112-jxxx.dtsi, which routes the front-left
USB-C port to dcpext and enables &dpaudio1. However, unlike the j473
Mac mini overlay, it never enables the SIO coprocessor (&sio) nor adds
the /aliases/sio entry.

m1n1 locates the SIO node via /aliases/sio in order to reserve its ASC
firmware region and load the coprocessor firmware. Without that alias,
m1n1's dt_setup_sio() silently skips the node, so even with status =
"okay" the coprocessor has no firmware and apple-sio fails with
"SIO did not boot" (-ETIME). The DP audio controller (dpaudio1) then has
no working DMA backend and no ALSA card is registered.

Add the sio alias and enable &sio/&dpaudio1, exactly as t8112-j473.dts.

Signed-off-by: paul <p4ulcristian@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j413.dts | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j413.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j413.dts
@@ -279,3 +279,28 @@
 };

 #include "hwmon-laptop.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * DisplayPort-altmode audio (USB-C DP monitors / AR glasses).
+ *
+ * The ENABLE_DCPEXT_TYPEC hack in t8112-jxxx.dtsi routes the front-left
+ * USB-C port to dcpext and enables dpaudio1, but leaves the SIO
+ * coprocessor disabled and, crucially, without an /aliases/sio entry.
+ * m1n1 locates the SIO via that alias to reserve and load its firmware;
+ * without it m1n1 skips SIO setup and the coprocessor fails to boot
+ * ("apple-sio: SIO did not boot").  Add the alias and enable the nodes,
+ * mirroring the t8112-j473 (Mac mini) overlay.
+ */
+/ {
+	aliases {
+		sio = &sio;
+	};
+};
+
+&sio {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&dpaudio1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
